# Bernoulli (Week 5)

Run `npm install`, then `npm start`. Run the calculation and API regression checks with `npm test`.

## Current-session quiz practice (Option A)

- Each tab session starts with an equal mix of the five taught topics. Only questions the learner asks in that session influence subsequent quiz selection. Questions are matched to the taught topics locally, once per send, including when the AI proxy is unavailable.
- Topic counts are held in `sessionStorage`: they survive a page reload within the tab session, without using other tabs, historical records, or the previous performance profile. A normally closed tab ends its session; browser session restoration may restore tab storage.
- Selection combines 40% balanced review with 60% session topic counts, starting with one prior count per topic. Every topic remains available. Quiz answers are scored and recorded but do not change topic weights.
- The focus panel, percentages, and manual topic selector are removed. **Start fresh** beside the coach title resets the session focus, anonymous identifier, chat display, scene, and quiz score. It does not delete server records or pending submissions. **Reset** continues to reset the scene and score only.
- Each question is scored once. Skipped questions do not count as incorrect. The scene is fixed during a quiz question so its values match the question and recorded result.
- If tab storage is unavailable, the session still works in memory until the page is reloaded or closed. No account or cross-device synchronization is required.

## Teaching records

Set `QUESTION_LOG_DIR` to the mounted Render persistent-disk directory. Chat/question logs remain in their existing files; first quiz submissions are appended to `quiz-attempts.jsonl` in the same directory. Quiz grading is recomputed from the submitted scene on the server. A learner/question pair is recorded once, including after retries or a server restart.

Quiz submissions waiting for a connection are retained in the browser and retried. The page shows pending-save status. The student recording notice covers questions, AI responses, and quiz answers.

CSV routes `/api/chat/export.csv`, `/api/questions/export.csv`, and `/api/quiz/export.csv` require the server's `INSTRUCTOR_TOKEN` in the `x-instructor-token` header. The separate local instructor download tool downloads all three files. There are no instructor controls on the student page. Historical quiz answers from before this feature were not recorded and cannot be reconstructed.
